![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If any of the required evidence (`plain`, `overlay`, or `model`) is missing or malformed, the script currently records a diagnostic but still returns the context object with these properties as `undefined`. This will cause unhandled `TypeError` exceptions downstream when trying to access properties like `context.plain.index`, `context.overlay.index`, or `context.model.index`.

To prevent these crashes and ensure the script fails closed gracefully, we should return `null` from `buildRowContexts` for any selected question that has missing required evidence, so it is filtered out of the returned array.

```javascript
    let hasMissingEvidence = false;
    for (const [role, value] of [
      ['plain_text_v2', plain],
      ['method_evidence_overlay', overlay],
      ['procedure_model_map', model],
    ]) {
      if (!value) {
        diagnostics.push({
          code: 'selected_question_missing_required_evidence',
          severity: 'critical',
          role,
          question_row_id: selection.question_row_id,
        });
        hasMissingEvidence = true;
      }
    }

    if (hasMissingEvidence) {
      return null;
    }

    return {
      selection,
      selectionIndex,
      source,
      overlay,
      plain,
      model,
      steps,
      receipt,
      objective,
    };
```

